text @[Tomoya]
text Nagisa...
text @[Tomoya]
text Sometimes I get scared.
sound N58.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Of what?
text @[Tomoya]
text When I think about what I'm living for.
sound N59.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text What you're living for?
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah...
music BGM01.mp3
text @[Tomoya]
text I was able to meet you, Nagisa.
text @[Tomoya]
text And... I was able to be with you.
text @[Tomoya]
text For me... I'm happy as long as I can be with you, making you happy.
text @[Tomoya]
text No matter how hard my work gets, I can keep on going, drenched in sweat.
text @[Tomoya]
text Because when I get home, you're there.
text @[Tomoya]
text Days like that are the one thing I can enjoy.
text @[Tomoya]
text So that makes me wonder. Is that what I'm living for?
text @[Tomoya]
text But I also think that all of this is just due to luck.
text @[Tomoya]
text What would I be doing right now if I'd never met you, Nagisa...?
text @[Tomoya]
text What kind of goals would I be trying to accomplish with my life?
text @[Tomoya]
text I don't have a family... or parents like yours...
text @[Tomoya]
text I wouldn't have friends after I graduated...
text @[Tomoya]
text I wouldn't have anyone to keep working alongside...
text @[Tomoya]
text No one to give me motivation...
text @[Tomoya]
text What would have driven me...?
text @[Tomoya]
text Looking at it from here, I don't think I would've been able to find any reason for living other than being together with you.
text @[Tomoya]
text So that makes me scared...
text @[Tomoya]
text Some people talk about fated meetings and stuff, but...
text @[Tomoya]
text I don't believe in that kind of thing.
text @[Tomoya]
text I think that in the end, it's all luck.
text @[Tomoya]
text I was just lucky to meet you, Nagisa.
text @[Tomoya]
text When I start thinking about that, it makes me feel like there's no shared, universal reason for living.
sound N5A.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text ...
sound N5B.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text If that had happened... then I'm sure that someone else would be by your side, Tomoya-kun.
text @[Tomoya]
text I wonder...
text @[Tomoya]
text I think I'd be alone.
text @[Tomoya]
text I don't think I would've wanted to be with anyone else.
text @[Tomoya]
text That's not something I'm just saying because I'm talking to you.
text @[Tomoya]
text That's really how I was back then.
text @[Tomoya]
text Maybe I would've ended up thinking a different way once I got older, but...
text @[Tomoya]
text I'd probably still be alone if I had never met you.
text @[Tomoya]
text And... I'd still be worried because of my father...
text @[Tomoya]
text Lost as to what to do with no support...
text What would've become of me if I'd never found something to live for?
text That thought is at the root of my fears.
text I feel like the vague mass that is life would've swallowed up my tiny little existence.
text It would've been... too overwhelming for me to fight back against.
text There's no point in screaming when you're all alone.
text I'd never be heard by some sort of greater power.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hey, Nagisa? Can I come over there...?
sound N5C.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Oh, yes... Go ahead.
text I get out of my futon and snuggle up to Nagisa.
text Her body is warm.
text For a while, we just stare at one another, not even making contact.
text After that, I end up hugging her.
text I wrap both of my arms around her tiny back and pull her toward me.
text My chest meets hers. It feels warm.
text I touch our foreheads together too, and then our noses.
text Nagisa smells wonderful.
text The person who supports me is so small, yet holding her like this makes me feel at ease, like a child.
text Yes, this is the kind of person I was able to meet.
text I was lucky.
text That's the truth.
text I should just accept it and not think too hard about it any longer.
text From now on, I should simply focus on protecting her.
text That's how I'll lead my life from this point forward.
text Yeah. That's right.
